    "hypothesis": "Replacing the failure-prone 16-bit two-pass scatter with a persistent-team four-pass 8-bit radix sort keeps per-thread histograms cache-resident and bounds scatter fan-out, reducing synchronization and cache-miss cost on four cores while retaining a sequential fallback for small arrays.",
    "notes": "Uses size_t bucket offsets and four passes so the final sorted data always resides in the caller array.",
